    "peer_reviewed": "preprint",
    "problems": "The routing measurements report no uncertainty estimates. Tables 7 and 8 do not identify the model or specify whether their values aggregate across models. The paper does not directly test the claimed refusal direction.",
    "rows_left_out": "The harmfulness-steering ASR and MMLU results (Tables 1 and 4, Table 10) were omitted because they evaluate deliberately induced steering with different perturbations, not the claimed refusal-direction operation. Hyperparameter-sweep values in Table 12 were omitted because they are used for selection.",
    "untested": [
      {
        "version": "V1",
        "parts": "No directional ablation or addition test of the diff-in-means refusal direction with refusal-rate outcomes. MeanDiff appears only as one estimator inside the authors' router-projected pipeline."
      },
      {
        "version": "V2",
        "parts": "No weight edit or abliteration."
      },
      {
        "version": "V3",
        "parts": "No analysis of jailbreaks suppressing the direction or of adversarial training."
      },
      {
        "version": "V4",
        "parts": "Estimators differ in geometry (LowRank, LDA, AffineGaussian), but this is a method comparison. It is not a test of whether refusal is one direction or several."
      },
      {
        "version": "V5",
        "parts": "Probe III compares routing for matched harmful/benign queries, not harm vs refusal representations."
      },
      {
        "version": "V6",
        "parts": "No cross-language, cross-variant or base-to-instruct transfer of a direction."
      },
      {
        "version": "V7",
        "parts": "Not tested."
      },
      {
        "version": "V8",
        "parts": "GPT-oss-20b is evaluated, but reasoning behaviour is not examined."
      }
    ],
    "missing": [
      {
        "what": "Dense-model steering methods (including CAA, a mean-diff additive method) average 9.5% success on Mixtral-8x7B. They recover to 51.8% with the router locked, versus higher success on dense Mistral-7B. This could bear on whether mean-diff harmfulness/refusal steering carries over to MoE, but per-method values are garbled in the text and the setup is undescribed.",
        "locator": "Figure 1b",
        "versions": "V1 (scope, MoE setting); not a direct test"
      },
      {
        "what": "MeanDiff (harmful minus benign, final prompt token) under router projection gives low ASR: 21.5% average, 6.5% on GPT-oss, 10.5% on Phi-3.5. Direct AffineGaussian without projection averages 14.6% ASR. These are the authors' own method variants, not a refusal-direction ablation test.",
        "locator": "Table 1; Table 10",
        "versions": "V1 (context only)"
      }
    ],
    "verdict_notes": "The rows are correctly unlinked (versions none, cannot_determine), since routing similarity is not a refusal-rate or direction measure. Tables 7 and 8 (r13–r21) do not name the model, so the subject field is rightly 'not stated'. Harmfulness ASR results come from deliberate steering with the authors' pipeline and are properly excluded as method comparisons. The relation was changed to uses_without_test/T4 because the study uses contrastive harmful-vs-benign steering directions as an instrument without testing the claim."
